@startuml
title Blueprint Gate: issue intake and worker context
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 120

participant "GitHub issues\n(external)" as GH #FFE6DB
participant "Control plane" as CP #DDEBFF
database "Job state" as DB #E8E8FF
participant "Host worker" as W #DFF3E3
collections "Issue worktree" as WT #DFF3E3
participant "Coding CLI" as CLI #FFF1D6
participant "Model provider\n(external)" as P #FFE6DB

CP -> GH: Poll issue + project state
GH --> CP: Issue text + metadata
note over GH, CP #FFF3CD
  Issue content crosses into the control plane as untrusted input.
  A signed webhook is an optional alternate intake path.
end note
CP -> DB: Ticket revision + queued stage
W -> CP: Claim + worker token + capabilities
note over W, CP #FFF3CD
  Local: loopback HTTP and shared token.
  Planned hybrid: HTTPS and scoped worker token.
  No worker is running yet.
end note
CP -> DB: Claim owner + fencing token
CP --> W: Stage job + issue/design artifacts + fence
W -> WT: Checkout + saved stage artifacts
W -> CLI: Stage prompt + selected context
note over W, CLI #FFF3CD
  Documented local startup exports the admin token.
  Child CLI processes inherit the worker environment.
  Provider receipt of that token is not established.
end note
CLI -> P: Prompt + selected work context
P --> CLI: Model response
CLI --> W: Generated artifact content
W -> WT: Save artifacts and changes
W -> CP: Completion + fence + result
CP -> DB: Persist result + next stage
@enduml
